  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Closest on Amazon: ProForm Pro 2000", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/brands/">Brands</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buyer’s Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">LifeSmart Treadmills: The PowerTouch Range Explained</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        LifeSmart treadmills are the self-folding PowerTouch machines you see at Costco and Dick’s Sporting Goods. The best-known of them, the TM4500, has been discontinued, and the range now runs from the TM3000 to the touchscreen TM6500, with Costco-only models alongside. This guide sets out what is current, what each model costs, which published figures disagree, and the one thing every buyer should know first: a one-year warranty.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 5, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#proform-pro-2000"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31M4plx9X1L._SL500_.jpg" alt="ProForm Pro 2000" width="500" height="446" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#lifesmart-tm3000"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/316uNl7L96L._SL500_.jpg" alt="LifeSmart TM3000" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#lifesmart-tm5000"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/4105NgoIU0L._SL500_.jpg" alt="LifeSmart TM5000" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>ProForm Pro 2000 · LifeSmart TM3000 · LifeSmart TM5000</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          LifeSmart's pitch is one feature: PowerTouch, a motorised fold that raises and lowers the deck at the press
          of a button, with infrared sensors meant to stop it lowering onto a pet or a child. Around that it builds
          brushless-motor folding treadmills with incline and a small decline, sold mainly through Costco and Dick's
          Sporting Goods and on its own store. The names are confusing — TM3000, TM3000C, TM4000, TM4000C, TM4500,
          TM4800, TM5000, TM6500, TM55, TM22X — and so are some of the figures. This guide sorts out which models are
          current, which are retailer-specific, what each one costs, and how a LifeSmart compares with similarly priced
          treadmills that carry much longer warranties.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest on Amazon:</span> <a href="#proform-pro-2000">ProForm Pro 2000</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Budget Pick:</span> <a href="#lifesmart-tm3000">LifeSmart TM3000</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Most Incline:</span> <a href="#lifesmart-tm5000">LifeSmart TM5000</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest on Amazon:</span> <a href="#nordictrack-t-series-16">NordicTrack T Series 16</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Closest on Amazon:</span> <a href="#nordictrack-commercial-1250">NordicTrack Commercial 1250</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[4].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          5 November 2026 we checked LifeSmart's US treadmill store (its full product catalogue with prices and stock
          flags, the TM3000, TM4000, TM4000C, TM4500 and TM5000 product pages, its warranty page and its About page),
          Costco's product pages for the TM6500 and TM55 (Costco's pages did not show prices to our requests, and its
          TM4500 page refused them), Action Lifestyle's TM4000C listing and a Costco deal tracker's TM4800 entry in
          search results, an open-box retailer's TM4800 listing, a fitness retailer's LifeSmart brand guide and Sole's
          blog coverage of the TM4500, and the US Consumer Product Safety Commission's recall database for LifeSmart.
          Several LifeSmart figures differ between LifeSmart, Costco and retailers; conflicts are set out in the text
          and kept off the cards, and where only LifeSmart publishes a figure we say so. Prices are those shown on the
          day and change often. The NordicTrack T Series 16 card, which stands in for the Costco-only TM6500, carries
          the figures checked for our NordicTrack treadmills guide; the ProForm Pro 2000 and NordicTrack Commercial
          1250 cards, which stand in for the TM4000C and TM4500 because we could not find them on Amazon US, carry the
          figures checked for our iFIT and NordicTrack guides. We have not tested any LifeSmart treadmill. As an Amazon Associate we earn from
          qualifying purchases; that does not change what we say.
        </aside>

